Z||000000||Tom88gt||01-16-2000||04:42 PM||||Well, I got my Fiero running again.  I replaced the coil and it fired right up.  Strange, since the old coil checked good on the ohm meter.  But there was nothing else left to replace.  Everything else for the ignition was replaced less than a month ago.<P>So if your car won't start and you have checked everything on the ignition, try replaceing the coil.<P>I can only guess that the coil had good continuity for an ohm test, just couldn't put out enough voltage to reach the plugs.  When I grounded the coil wire I got a spark.  I guess it just wasn't powerfull enough to make it to the plugs.||||reg||6
